comdlg32: select the proposed file name when the item dialog opens

IFileDialog's dialog (itemdlg) puts the proposed name (IFileDialog::SetFileName,
e.g. Notepad++'s "new 1") into the name field and gives the field the focus by
SetFocus(), which leaves the caret at the start and nothing selected: a name
typed right away goes in front of the proposed one ("mynamenew 1.txt"). On
Windows the proposed name is selected and typing replaces it.

The field's text is now selected after it gets the focus.

--- a/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
+++ b/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
@@ -2192,7 +2192,11 @@
         events_OnTypeChange(This);
 
     if ((hitem = GetDlgItem(This->dlg_hwnd, IDC_FILENAME)))
+    {
         SetFocus(hitem);
+        /* as Windows: the proposed name is selected, so a typed name replaces it */
+        SendMessageW(hitem, EM_SETSEL, 0, -1);
+    }
 
     return FALSE;
 }
